Subject: [PATCH] spl: repair the cyclic list head after moving global data

SPL may register cyclic callbacks before relocating its stack and global
data to DRAM. Copying global data moves the hlist head but leaves the first
callback's pprev pointing to the original head in SRAM. Removing that
callback then updates the old head, leaving the new list with a stale
entry; unregistering a watchdog before FEL exposes this.

Repoint the first callback at the copied head, as required by the hlist
layout. Subsequent callbacks already point at their predecessor nodes and
need no adjustment.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/common/spl/spl.c b/common/spl/spl.c
--- a/common/spl/spl.c
+++ b/common/spl/spl.c
@@ -953,6 +953,11 @@
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(DM)
 	dm_fixup_for_gd_move(new_gd);
 #endif
+#if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(CYCLIC)
+	/* The first callback still points back to the old list head. */
+	if (new_gd->cyclic_list.first)
+		new_gd->cyclic_list.first->pprev = &new_gd->cyclic_list.first;
+#endif
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(LOG)
 	log_fixup_for_gd_move(new_gd);
 #endif
